slots.doc:
Puts a view at the top of the list, above the first row, such as a strip of notes. It
scrolls with the rows.

The view spans the list's width with no insets and no separators; draw a divider in it if
you want one. It is not a row: it does not open a channel and has no swipe actions. Buttons
inside it take only their own taps, because the screen gives it the borderless button
style; a style you set inside the view wins. Pagination is not affected.

It shows while the channels load, when there are none, and when loading failed, since its
content is your own data. The loading indicator, the empty message, and the error with
Retry stay centered over the list; if the header is tall enough to reach the middle of the
list, they draw over it. The closure runs again when you redraw the list with new data.

```swift
ChannelListView()
    .channelListHeader {
        ScrollView(.horizontal, showsIndicators: false) {
            HStack {
                ForEach(notes) { note in NoteBubble(note) }
            }
            .padding(.horizontal, 16)
        }
    }
```

- Since: 1.0.0

Replaces the default centered header with a view at the leading edge of the navigation bar.

The view is shown at its ideal size, so the navigation bar does
not clip it and you do not need `.fixedSize()`. Long text is not truncated for you: give
the text an explicit width with `.frame(width:)` and a `lineLimit` to cap it. The bar does
not grow, so keep the view within its height; a picture, a name, and a one-line subtitle fit.

```swift
ChannelView(channel: channel)
    .channelHeader { channel in
        VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 0) {
            Text(channel.name ?? "Chat").font(.headline)
            Text("Active now").font(.caption).foregroundStyle(.secondary)
        }
    }
```

Return no view to hide the header. The screen then adds no item at the leading edge, so a
`toolbar` item of your own takes that spot. The default channel name below the bar stays
hidden, as it does whenever this slot is set:

```swift
ChannelView(channel: channel)
    .channelHeader { _ in EmptyView() }
    .toolbar {
        ToolbarItem(placement: .topBarLeading) {
            Button("Chats", systemImage: "line.3.horizontal") { showsChats = true }
        }
    }
```

